        "PMC7311485::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC7311485::web::009::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tribolayer reduces effective interfacial shear strength.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7311485::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tribolayer acts as a protective barrier against wear.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7311485::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial CoCrFeMnNi material has a coarse-grained microstructure.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7311485::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC7311485::web::009::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The initial CoCrFeMnNi coating has no pre-formed protective tribolayer.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "High local contact stress during sliding dynamically refines grains in the near-surface region.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7311485::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "High local contact stress during sliding causes near-surface amorphization.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7311485::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The resulting tribolayer is continuous and stable.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Near-surface ultra-nanocrystalline layer formation is associated with low friction in CoCrFeMnNi under UHV sliding.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7311485::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Near-surface ultra-nanocrystalline layer formation mitigates material removal and lowers wear.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7311485::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC7311485::web::009::results_and_discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Moderately increasing normal load makes the tribolayer form earlier and more uniformly.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Moderately increasing normal load decreases friction relative to the low-load baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The expected friction coefficient is approximately 0.2 to 0.3.",
